 2. 💰 AI boom transforms philanthropy 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The AI boom is about to rewrite the rules of global philanthropy, shifting its center of gravity to Silicon Valley, where the IPOs of AI giants Anthropic and OpenAI will create some of the world's largest charitable organizations, Axios' Bradley Olson writes. 

 Why it matters: The new wave will mirror startup culture, dominated by flexible capital, ambitious bets and a search for measurable impact rather than old-school donations to rename hospital wings or graduate programs. 💰 Zoom in: Anthropic announced yesterday that it plans to launch a massive benefit fund with 5% of its shares.

 The company's pledge, which would amount to $100 billion if it reaches an IPO value of $2 trillion , will go to a public benefit fund and is set to grow as its valuation rises. Anthropic says the fund will be a wholly owned LLC, giving it flexibility to make large donations to nonprofits or distribute money directly to specific populations.

 The commitment builds on the pledges of co-founders to give away 80% of their equity. 🖼️ The big picture: Anthropic is joining OpenAI, which is controlled by a nonprofit foundation that holds a 26% equity stake in the company, worth about $130 billion based on the company's current valuation.

