 3. 🇺🇦 Zelensky&#x27;s olive branch 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Volodymyr Zelensky meets King Charles at Buckingham Palace last week. Photo: Aaron Chown/Press Association via Reuters 🇷🇺 Breaking: Vladimir Putin has proposed a three-way summit next month with President Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping in an effort to negotiate an end to the Ukraine war on terms favorable to Russia, although Trump hasn't agreed, The Wall Street Journal reports ( gift link ). 

 Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky spoke yesterday with Trump envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner about the crisis between the countries and U.S. efforts to resume peace talks with Russia, Axios' Barak Ravid reports. 

 During the call, which lasted around 40 minutes, Zelensky discussed the possibility of holding an in-person meeting in the coming days. Why it matters: It was the first call between Zelensky and senior U.S. officials since tensions spiked after Trump cut a diesel deal with Russia 10 days ago.

 The latest: Trump defended his decision to grant a waiver related to sanctions pushed by the late Sen. Lindsey Graham (R-S.C.), saying the U.S. didn't want to jeopardize negotiations with Russia.

 "I am in the process of negotiating Peace in the war between Russia and Ukraine, and don't want to do anything that will drive, foolishly, Russia away from the bargaining table," Trump wrote on Truth Social. Read more . 

 
 
