 4. 💊 Health stocks boom 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: FactSet. Chart: Axios/Matt Phillips Health care stocks have done well in recent months as investors bank on Democrats gaining power in the midterm elections, Axios Markets co-author Matt Phillips writes. 

 Why it matters: The prices suggest traders and investors see increasing odds that some cuts to federal health spending imposed by President Trump's big 2025 spending bill could be undone. The S&amp;P 500's health care sector is up more than 9% over the last three months, the second-best performer of the blue-chip index's 11 sectors. (Energy was the best.)

 Pharmaceutical shares like Eli Lilly, Merck and AbbVie were some of the strong contributors. Sign up for Axios Markets . 

 
 
