 8. 🍅 1 film thing: Holmes movie hits ratings heights 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Elizabeth Holmes in "You Can See Everything." Image: A24 "You Can See Everything," the Elizabeth Holmes pseudo-documentary from Nathan Fielder, reached a 100% rating on Rotten Tomatoes, making it the highest-rated movie of the year on the review site, Forbes reports.

 Though a single negative review dropped the movie to 99% as of Sunday night, it still tops every other 2026 film. At the box office, the movie brought in $15 million in its debut weekend — remarkable for a documentary, Variety reports . 🍿 A particularly cringeworthy scene from the movie's trailer became one of the year's biggest internet memes , and it's being credited with driving young audiences to see the film.

